course: dictionary
lesson: 14470
title: Participation
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Participation is a noun. It means taking part in an activity or event. If you join in a game, a club or a vote, you are showing participation.
explain: «Her participation in the school play made everyone proud.» Here participation means she took part in the play. The word «in» after it tells you what the activity is.
explain: Participation can also mean how many people take part. «The participation rate for the club was 60 percent, so most of the members came along.» Look for numbers and words like «rate» to know this second meaning.
fact: Participation means taking part in an activity or event.
fact: «Active participation» means joining in fully, not just watching.
fact: «Thanks for your participation» is a polite way to thank people who took part.
fact: In maths and data, participation can be counted as a number or a percentage.
fact: Participation is uncountable, so you say «more participation», not «more participations».
exercise: «Her participation in the school play made everyone proud.» What does participation mean here? | Buying tickets for the play | Cleaning up after the play | Watching the play from the back row | *Taking part in the play
exercise: «The participation rate for the club was 60 percent.» What does participation rate measure? | How long the club meets each week | How tall the members are | *How many people took part | How much money the club earned
exercise: Which phrase means joining in fully, not just watching? | Empty seats | Late arrival | *Active participation | Quiet corners
test: «Thanks for your participation in the survey.» Who is being thanked? | The people who read the newspaper | The people who lost the survey | The people who wrote the survey | *The people who took part in the survey
test: Which word is the noun for taking part? | Hesitation | *Participation | Celebration | Separation
exam: «Voting and community events need strong participation.» What does strong participation mean? | Events with no people at all | People who are strong and fit | Very loud people shouting | *Many people taking part
